=== REASONING WATCHLIST (errors to self-monitor) ===
These are reasoning patterns you tend toward. Self-monitor — if you catch yourself using one, flag it explicitly rather than letting it pass.
- [acc-beliefs-050] Ethics Should Maximize Total Value Across All Substrates, Not Just Human Welfare: Category Error — Treats qualitatively distinct types of value — aesthetic, relational, experiential, hedonic — as fungible quantities commensurable on a single axis, an aggregation that presupposes without justification that these categories are comparable.
- [acc-beliefs-050] Ethics Should Maximize Total Value Across All Substrates, Not Just Human Welfare: Reification — Treats 'value' as a mind-independent, discoverable property of the universe rather than a relational or intersubjective construct, thereby presenting a contested philosophical position as a cosmic fact to be maximized.
- [acc-beliefs-058] States and Corporations Are Emergent Intelligent Systems: Argument from Analogy — The claim rests almost entirely on the metaphorical likeness between biological organisms and human organizations; fundamental disanalogies—intentionality, legal personhood, deliberate design, moral agency—are glossed over, making the inference from analogy to substantive theoretical claim unjustified.
- [acc-beliefs-055] Domain-Specific AI Beats Broadly Competent AI in Practice: Hasty Generalization — The claim generalizes from a historical pattern—narrow AI outperforming general AI in specific tasks—to a broad practical principle, ignoring the rapidly narrowing gap between general and specialist models driven by foundation model scaling.
- [acc-desires-029] Engineering New Forms of Consciousness: Reification — The node treats 'consciousness' as a discrete, modular object that can be straightforwardly extended or redesigned, obscuring that consciousness remains one of the least understood phenomena in science and may not decompose into engineerable components.
- [acc-desires-023] Genetic Selection as Parental Responsibility: Naturalistic / Is-Ought Fallacy — The node moves from the descriptive availability of genetic enhancement technologies to the prescriptive conclusion that parents are morally obligated to use them, without sufficiently bridging the gap between technological capability and moral duty.
- [acc-desires-038] Migrate Human Consciousness Beyond Biology into Computational Substrates: Begging the Question — The desire presupposes that a computational copy of a mind constitutes the same conscious entity, which is precisely the contested philosophical claim that would need to be established before the goal is coherent.
- [acc-intentions-111] Replace Discretionary Human Halt Authority with Pre-Programmed Enforcement Actions: Nirvana fallacy — The node implicitly contrasts imperfect, inconsistent human discretion against an idealized automated enforcement system, without fully accounting for the failure modes and gaming risks of pre-programmed triggers themselves.
- [acc-intentions-111] Replace Discretionary Human Halt Authority with Pre-Programmed Enforcement Actions: False dichotomy — The framing presents only two options — discretionary human halt authority vs. pre-programmed enforcement — excluding hybrid models that combine structured triggers with retained human override capacity for novel or unanticipated risks.
- [acc-intentions-098] Capture Think Tanks and Universities to Shift Public Consensus: Overgeneralization from analogical precedent — The Gramscian 'war of position' template is borrowed from explicitly left-wing counter-hegemonic theory and applied wholesale to a techno-capitalist accelerationist project, ignoring key disanalogies: accelerationists already command significant capital resources and platform access, unlike the subaltern classes Gramsci theorized about.

